[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: GHOST MCP ActiveBlackboard Requirements
UID: GHOST-MCP-ACTIVEBLACKBOARD
VERSION: 0.1-draft
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text
  AUTO_LEVELS: On
  NODE_IN_TOC: True

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Purpose and Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document owns all GHOST MCP requirements concerning ActiveBlackboard.

It deliberately contains two different maturity levels:

1. Current implemented Persistent Chat prototype behavior.
2. Future ActiveBlackboard vision.

The Persistent Chat implementation is the first executable stage toward ActiveBlackboard and shall be documented as implementation fact.

The final multi-chat and multi-actor ActiveBlackboard architecture is not yet fully designed. Future requirements therefore remain high-level and shall not invent unresolved coordination semantics.

No ActiveBlackboard behavior belongs in 111_mcp_capabilities.sdoc.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-ROOT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: ActiveBlackboard Scope
STATEMENT: >>>
GHOST shall maintain a dedicated MCP requirement area for ActiveBlackboard.

The requirement area shall distinguish:

- current Persistent Chat behavior that already exists; and
- future shared ActiveBlackboard behavior that remains under design.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 2. Current Persistent Chat Prototype

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The current implementation provides Persistent Chat Memory as a single-stream prototype of ActiveBlackboard.

It uses the common GHOST memory infrastructure while applying a dedicated MCP persistence policy.

The implementation is currently centered on three tools:

- ghost_persistent_chat_init
- ghost_persistent_chat_append
- ghost_persistent_chat_resume

These names describe current executable behavior and shall not be replaced in the requirements by hypothetical future tool names.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-CURRENT-PROTOTYPE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Persistent Chat as ActiveBlackboard Prototype
STATEMENT: >>>
The current Persistent Chat implementation shall be treated as the first executable ActiveBlackboard prototype.

It validates:

- explicit activation of persistent conversation recording;
- one persistent history across multiple conversation turns;
- append-only visible Q/A recording;
- cumulative ActiveBrief continuity;
- deterministic resume; and
- owner-scoped persistent state.

It shall not be represented as the final multi-actor ActiveBlackboard architecture.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-CURRENT-SINGLE-STREAM
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Current Single-Stream Boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The current Persistent Chat implementation shall be treated as a single continuing chat stream.

Its use of ActiveBlackboard-related storage naming shall not by itself establish implemented multi-chat, multi-actor, shared-board, or agent-coordination behavior.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-CURRENT-PROTOTYPE

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. Persistent Chat Initialization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-INIT-TOOL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Persistent Chat Initialize Tool
STATEMENT: >>>
The current MCP server shall expose:

ghost_persistent_chat_init

Initialization shall explicitly create one new persistent chat memory for the authenticated owner.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-CURRENT-PROTOTYPE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-INIT-EXPLICIT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Persistent Recording Requires Explicit Activation
STATEMENT: >>>
Persistent Chat recording shall begin only after an explicit successful initialization or resume operation.

Ordinary conversation before activation shall not be represented as automatically persisted by this capability.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-INIT-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-INIT-INPUT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Initialization Identity
STATEMENT: >>>
Initialization shall require a user-provided title.

A general memory description may also be supplied.

The implementation shall not invent unsupported project facts merely to populate an optional description.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-INIT-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-STABLE-ID
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Stable Persistent Memory Identity
STATEMENT: >>>
Initialization shall create one stable persistent memory identity.

The current implementation exposes this identity as file_id.

The same persistent memory shall continue across dates and later resume operations rather than being split into a new daily conversation memory.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-INIT-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-INIT-NO-EPISODE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Initialization Does Not Save a Conversation Episode
STATEMENT: >>>
Initialization shall create the persistent memory history but shall not fabricate or save a conversation episode.

The first episode shall be created only by a subsequent successful append.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-INIT-TOOL

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Persistent Chat Append

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-APPEND-TOOL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Persistent Chat Append Tool
STATEMENT: >>>
The current MCP server shall expose:

ghost_persistent_chat_append

The operation shall append one normal visible user/assistant exchange to an already initialized persistent chat memory.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-CURRENT-PROTOTYPE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-VISIBLE-QA
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Persist Complete Visible Q/A
STATEMENT: >>>
Each appended episode shall contain:

- the complete visible user message; and
- the substantive visible assistant answer produced for that user message.

The persistence path shall not intentionally replace the visible exchange with a summary.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-APPEND-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-NO-HIDDEN-CONTENT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Hidden Processing Is Not Conversation Content
STATEMENT: >>>
Persistent Chat shall not save as conversation content:

- hidden chain-of-thought;
- internal model reasoning;
- MCP protocol traffic;
- internal tool results;
- hidden tool arguments;
- internal application diagnostics; or
- the GHOST persistence receipt itself.

Only the visible conversation content selected by the approved append behavior shall form the saved Q/A episode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-VISIBLE-QA

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-PRESENTATION-AUTHORITY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Client Remains Answer Presentation Authority
STATEMENT: >>>
The invoking AI client shall compose the normal complete answer for the user before that answer is persisted.

GHOST Persistent Chat shall store the supplied answer and shall not become a replacement answer renderer.

Normal Markdown, code blocks, tables, and other visible answer formatting may remain part of the persisted assistant response.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-VISIBLE-QA

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-ANSWER-BEFORE-APPEND
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Answer Then Persist
STATEMENT: >>>
The intended visible interaction order shall be:

1. compose the normal assistant answer;
2. append the same substantive visible Q/A to Persistent Chat;
3. receive the GHOST save result; and
4. present the normal answer followed by the short persistence receipt when appropriate.

The persistence receipt shall not become part of the saved assistant answer.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-PRESENTATION-AUTHORITY

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-APPEND-EXISTING-ONLY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Append Does Not Create Missing Persistent Memory
STATEMENT: >>>
ghost_persistent_chat_append shall operate only on an existing owner-scoped Persistent Chat memory.

Append failure shall not silently initialize a new persistent memory.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-APPEND-TOOL

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. ActiveBrief Continuity

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-ACTIVEBRIEF
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Cumulative ActiveBrief
STATEMENT: >>>
Each successfully appended Persistent Chat episode shall contain the current cumulative ActiveBrief.

The ActiveBrief shall represent the useful cumulative conversation state required to continue the persistent chat.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-APPEND-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-FIRST-BRIEF
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Initial ActiveBrief
STATEMENT: >>>
For the first persisted episode, the invoking AI client shall compose the initial ActiveBrief from that first visible Q/A.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-ACTIVEBRIEF

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-BRIEF-UPDATE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: ActiveBrief Update
STATEMENT: >>>
For each later episode, the invoking AI client shall construct the updated cumulative ActiveBrief from:

- the previous latest ActiveBrief; and
- the current visible user/assistant exchange.

The resulting ActiveBrief shall represent the updated cumulative state after the new episode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-ACTIVEBRIEF

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-CLIENT-BRIEF-AUTHORITY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Client-Composed ActiveBrief
STATEMENT: >>>
The current Persistent Chat prototype shall rely on the invoking AI client to compose the updated ActiveBrief.

GHOST persistence code shall store the supplied ActiveBrief and shall not require a separate GHOST LLM call merely to recreate the same cumulative summary.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-ACTIVEBRIEF

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. Episode Ordering and Persistence Integrity

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-SEQUENCE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Persistent Episode Sequence
STATEMENT: >>>
Each appended Persistent Chat episode shall have deterministic sequence ordering within its persistent memory.

The current implementation stores sequence_number and links a new episode to the preceding episode through parent_id.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-APPEND-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-STREAM-ID
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Persistent Chat Stream Identity
STATEMENT: >>>
Current Persistent Chat episodes shall remain traceable to their persistent stream.

The current implementation stores the stable persistent file_id as the chat_stream_id for appended episodes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-SEQUENCE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RECORD-ID
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Stable Episode Record ID
STATEMENT: >>>
Each persisted episode shall have a stable Record ID.

The Record ID shall be returned in the successful persistence receipt and shall remain usable as an exact handle for deterministic resume.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-APPEND-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-COMMON-PERSISTENCE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Common GHOST Persistence Infrastructure
STATEMENT: >>>
The current Persistent Chat implementation shall use the established GHOST durable memory infrastructure:

- MemoryRecord;
- .ragmem;
- .ragmeta.json;
- shared SQLite indexing; and
- stable file_id / record_id identities.

Persistent Chat shall not require a parallel unrelated persistence format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-CURRENT-PROTOTYPE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-COHERENCE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Body Metadata and Index Coherence
STATEMENT: >>>
Before continuing or resuming an existing Persistent Chat memory, the current implementation shall validate coherence among the durable memory body, metadata file, and SQLite index sufficiently to avoid continuing from an inconsistent identity or episode set.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-COMMON-PERSISTENCE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-PARTIAL-SAVE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Partial Save Shall Not Be Reported as Success
STATEMENT: >>>
If durable episode body data has been written but a later metadata or SQLite update fails, GHOST shall not claim that the episode was coherently saved.

The failure result may identify the durable Record ID so recovery or repair remains possible.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-COMMON-PERSISTENCE

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 7. Persistent Chat Resume

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RESUME-TOOL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Persistent Chat Resume Tool
STATEMENT: >>>
The current MCP server shall expose:

ghost_persistent_chat_resume

Resume shall locate an existing owner-scoped Persistent Chat memory through an exact previously persisted episode Record ID.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-CURRENT-PROTOTYPE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RESUME-NO-CREATE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Resume Never Creates a Memory
STATEMENT: >>>
A failed resume request shall not initialize or fabricate a new Persistent Chat memory.

Resume is a deterministic recovery operation over already existing persistent state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RESUME-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RESUME-OWNER
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Owner-Scoped Resume
STATEMENT: >>>
A Record ID used for resume shall resolve only within the authenticated owner's Persistent Chat memories.

A Record ID belonging to another owner shall not expose or resume that owner's persistent memory.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RESUME-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RESUME-LATEST
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Resume From Latest Coherent State
STATEMENT: >>>
The supplied Record ID shall identify the Persistent Chat history.

After that history is identified, continuation shall use the latest coherent episode and latest cumulative ActiveBrief belonging to that history, even when newer episodes exist after the supplied resume handle.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RESUME-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RESUME-STATE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Resume State
STATEMENT: >>>
A successful resume shall provide sufficient state for continued persistence, including:

- stable persistent file_id;
- title;
- description where present;
- latest Record ID;
- latest sequence number;
- latest episode time; and
- latest cumulative ActiveBrief.

The exact current response schema may additionally expose related metadata already present in the implementation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PCHAT-RESUME-LATEST

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 8. List and Delete Integration

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-LIST-TARGET
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: ActiveBlackboard Participation in Generic List
STATEMENT: >>>
ActiveBlackboard memories shall participate in the shared generic memory List capability when that capability is extended to the final memory model.

List shall expose metadata and navigation information rather than automatically returning complete persistent-chat histories.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-EPISODE-DELETE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Individual ActiveBlackboard Episode Delete
STATEMENT: >>>
An individual ActiveBlackboard/Persistent Chat episode may be deleted through the shared deterministic memory Delete capability using an exact Record ID or other approved exact selector.

Semantic or descriptive deletion shall not be used.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-DELETE-BRIEF-TRACE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: ActiveBrief Residual Trace After Episode Delete
STATEMENT: >>>
Deleting an individual historical ActiveBlackboard episode does not require rewriting all later cumulative ActiveBriefs.

A later ActiveBrief may therefore preserve a summarized trace of information that originated in the deleted episode.

This residual cumulative-summary effect is accepted for individual episode deletion.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-EPISODE-DELETE

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 9. Current Prototype Boundary

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-NO-CURRENT-MULTIACTOR
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: No Current Multi-Actor Blackboard Claim
STATEMENT: >>>
The current Persistent Chat prototype shall not be represented as implementing:

- several cooperating actor streams;
- autonomous Blackboard agents;
- Programmer/Auditor/Architect/Requirements coordination;
- shared multi-chat routing;
- background Blackboard orchestration; or
- a completed shared-board GUI.

Those capabilities belong to the future ActiveBlackboard vision.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-CURRENT-PROTOTYPE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-NO-INVENTED-CURRENT-TOOLS
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: No Invented Current Lifecycle Tools
STATEMENT: >>>
Current implementation documentation shall identify the executable Persistent Chat tools as Init, Append, and Resume.

Verify, Close, actor-routing, board-synchronization, or other hypothetical lifecycle tools shall not be claimed as implemented unless corresponding code and requirements are later approved.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-CURRENT-PROTOTYPE

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 10. Future ActiveBlackboard Vision

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The following requirements deliberately preserve only the approved future direction.

They do not define the final ActiveBlackboard protocol.

Detailed coordination semantics remain open until explicitly designed and approved.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-SHARED
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Shared Ongoing Blackboard
STATEMENT: >>>
A future ActiveBlackboard shall support ongoing shared work context spanning more than one participating chat or specialist actor.

The Blackboard shall provide durable continuity so participating actors can work from shared project state rather than depending solely on one native client conversation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-ACTORS
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Multiple Specialist Actors
STATEMENT: >>>
Future ActiveBlackboard participants may include specialist roles such as:

- Programmer;
- Auditor;
- Architect;
- Requirements; and
- other explicitly defined actors.

Actor roles shall remain identifiable so their contributions can be inspected and traced.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-SHARED

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-BRIEFS
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Future Actor or Stream ActiveBriefs
STATEMENT: >>>
A future ActiveBlackboard may maintain cumulative ActiveBrief state for individual actors, chat streams, or another explicitly designed Blackboard scope.

The final rule for shared versus per-actor versus per-stream ActiveBriefs is not yet approved and shall not be invented by this requirement.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-SHARED

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-PULL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Pull-Based Shared Context Direction
STATEMENT: >>>
The approved future direction favors actors retrieving relevant shared Blackboard state when needed rather than assuming uncontrolled automatic broadcast of all state to all actors.

The exact retrieval and routing algorithm remains unresolved.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-SHARED

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-GUI
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Future Blackboard Workbench
STATEMENT: >>>
A future GHOST workbench may provide a Blackboard-oriented view of:

- sessions;
- streams;
- actors;
- titles;
- timestamps;
- saved episodes; and
- relevant cumulative state.

The workbench direction may support human-controlled filtering, searching, editing, tagging, archiving, and movement of information between appropriate contexts.

Detailed GUI implementation remains outside the current MCP protocol contract.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-SHARED

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-HUMAN-CONTROL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Human-Controlled Blackboard
STATEMENT: >>>
The future ActiveBlackboard shall remain inspectable and under human control.

Shared state, actor participation, persistence, and future coordination shall not become an opaque autonomous source of authority over the user's current request.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-FUTURE-SHARED

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 11. Intentionally Unresolved Future Design

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-UNRESOLVED
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: ActiveBlackboard Detailed Architecture Is Open
STATEMENT: >>>
The following future ActiveBlackboard decisions are intentionally unresolved:

- exact actor coordination protocol;
- exact actor-routing algorithm;
- shared versus per-actor versus per-stream ActiveBrief ownership;
- final Blackboard lifecycle operations;
- automatic versus user-triggered synchronization;
- exact shared-state selection semantics;
- exact conflict-handling behavior;
- final future MCP tool schemas; and
- final future GUI interaction model.

These details shall not be invented in requirements until explicitly designed and approved.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-NO-FUTURE-IMPLEMENTATION-CLAIM
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Future Vision Is Not Current Implementation
STATEMENT: >>>
The existence of the working Persistent Chat prototype shall not be used as evidence that the unresolved multi-chat or multi-actor ActiveBlackboard vision has already been implemented.

Current implementation claims shall remain limited to verified Persistent Chat behavior.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-BLACKBOARD-UNRESOLVED

[[/SECTION]]
